# Cyrius Field Notes — Compiler Internal Gotchas
# Non-obvious traps an agent will hit when working on cyrius's
# compiler internals: regalloc, layout, alignment, IR ordering,
# heap caps, fn-table conventions, codegen-vs-IR divergence.
#
# Earn their slot when an agent is debugging a cyrius
# regression that doesn't fit a clean pattern. The shape is
# always "this surprised future-me; here's the diagnosis +
# fix + how to recognize it again."
#
# For process methodology see methodology.cyml.
# For design patterns see patterns.cyml.
# For full backstory + chronological context see retros/.
#
# ⚠ `vr01_` IN OLDER ENTRIES IS A HISTORICAL FILENAME, NOT AN INSTRUCTION. That prefix
#   selected the cross-OS corpus until v6.5.11; the selector is now the
#   `tests/tcyr/crossos/` DIRECTORY and zero `vr01_*` files remain. Naming a new test
#   `vr01_*` today opts it OUT of the release gate's cross-OS leg — the opposite of what
#   the prefix used to mean. Live paths were repaired at the v6.6.1 audit; remaining
#   mentions are inside narratives about bugs found when the file was called that.
#
# 190 entries at 6.7.15 (DERIVED, the same grep). 6.7.15 added SIX, one per lane that met compiler gotchas —
# type_argument_lists_pointer_binding_and_once_per_site_diagnostics_v6715 (generics), frontend_redeclarations_baked_
# literals_and_refused_names_v6715, infratools_mode_pairs_key_tables_asm_operands_and_the_linear_seed_pass_v6715,
# forward_call_signatures_dereference_copies_and_inline_str_destinations_v6715 (structs, with the wave-2 merge's semantic
# conflict), vector_receives_one_recogniser_inline_frames_and_pointer_typing_v6715, receives_known_callee_records_
# assignment_judge_and_zone_sweep_v6715; the platform lane's went INTO class entries, as did the rest: the emitted-bytes
# class (its 14th: a fold over a node another pass marked), the syscall-number class (#12 closed: cxvm serves a guest's
# calls through the host's wrappers), a cap believed in five places (its 14th: a truncating key store and a whole-key
# compare), cybs (the last fn's locals, the include-once list's width and its qword stores), two passes (the `**` pin
# read, a zone generic instance minted at the sweep, signatures re-read once every struct is registered), a stated cause
# (five more), the green gate (an empty build output cmp-equals itself), the inline-replay frame entry (its open half
# closed, VC-1), unhandled flags (the TS front end on every fork), the PE errno entry (a BOOL folded, the std-fd map, r9,
# the include NAME rule, a fn-local const), and the filed halves of the 6.7.14 lane entries and of typed_subscripts #1 /
# struct_destinations #5, each marked closed where it stood.
# 184 entries at 6.7.14 (DERIVED, the same grep). 6.7.14 added NINE, one per lane — ir_arena_dce_ranges_and_the_instruction_
# aligned_call_graph_v6714 (infra), generic_names_type_arguments_and_once_per_token_errors_v6714 (generics),
# frontend_cascade_latches_direct_reports_and_the_bake_v6714, tools_lane_forwarded_children_predicted_temps_and_inherited_
# ignores_v6714, pe_errno_stubs_region_declarations_and_the_ctl_signature_hash_v6714 (platform), struct_values_shared_
# readers_and_inline_str_copies_v6714, receives_multi_value_capture_first_and_pass1_counts_v6714, cx_guest_branch_reach_
# vm_bounds_and_the_lib_leaf_order_v6714 (stdlib), vector_values_win64_parity_inline_frames_and_post_parse_types_v6714;
# the rest went INTO class entries: the emitted-bytes class (its 11th - 13th: a field emit and a float literal IR=3 was
# not told about, a byte scan read as a call graph; the PE errno stubs), compaction (a range recorded before the IR=3
# seam, CYRIUS_SYMS, the realign pad), phase0 (a grow that drops a copy, a reader on the fixed base), a cap believed in
